  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-dual-auto",
      "text": "**Dual-model auto-routing plugin for the DeepSeek Harness (dsh).**\n\nLow-cost direct / high-cost upgrade with an escape-learning closed loop."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm add @lengquan88/dsh-dual-auto\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Enable",
      "text": "Add one row to your profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n- insert:\n    - id: dual-auto\n      name: '@lengquan88/dsh-dual-auto'\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`. The tools `dual_model_route`, `dual_model_run`, and\n`dual_model_mark` become available in every session."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `dual_model_route` | Six-criteria routing decision (length / context / domain coverage / rule conflict / confidence / novelty → six labels). Fingerprints that escaped once are force-upgraded. |\n| `dual_model_run` | Decision + real model call: `direct` → `deepseek-v4-flash`, `upgrade` → `deepseek-v4-pro` (auto-degrade to flash on failure, marked `degraded`). Probe tasks auto-validate against a gold set — wrong direct answers trigger escape learning. |\n| `dual_model_mark` | Mark the quality of a direct result. `correct=false` learns the fingerprint and rewrites the disk log marker; the same fingerprint is force-upgraded next time. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Persistence",
      "text": "State persists to `output/dsh_router_{fingerprints,stats}.json` and\n`dsh_router_decision_log.jsonl` — interoperable with the project's Python\n`dao/model_router.py` (v2 dict fingerprints load directly)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Links",
      "text": "- npm: <https://www.npmjs.com/package/@lengquan88/dsh-dual-auto>\n- Source mirror (atomgit): <https://atomgit.com/guaikepa/zhonghua/tree/main/dsh-dual-auto>"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
